{"skill":{"slug":"openai-whisper-api","displayName":"Openai Whisper Api"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545368103,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"scripts/transcribe.sh","size":1479,"sha256":"06d255cdd1a44ea3098ca1d9400529c641da76b4e9389007904f190e681d5688","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1093,"sha256":"4cd90ed4d059a385948ffbf2896764a7db66dfbd06010d699b269e89e3f586be","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1730,"sha256":"c28cac3b9d6620d7e036c36d9f407f8a732ab46816ba721fc2067d6ff9645406","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013665129,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5ff836cb938859d25922ce56efad9212ecdd4f4fc82703168d02b2a338129e8d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5ff836cb938859d25922ce56efad9212ecdd4f4fc82703168d02b2a338129e8d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: openai-whisper-api\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to a local file write vulnerability in `scripts/transcribe.sh`. The `--out` parameter allows the user to specify an arbitrary file path for the transcription output, which could lead to overwriting sensitive files (e.g., configuration files, startup scripts) if the user has write permissions to those locations. While the skill's primary purpose is legitimate, this lack of output path validation presents a significant security risk, potentially enabling data corruption or persistence if exploited by a malicious actor.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159620171},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":42,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789013665129},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward OpenAI transcription helper, but users should understand that selected audio is uploaded to OpenAI with their API key.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, an OpenAI API key, and access to the chosen audio file are proportionate for remote transcription, but audio may contain sensitive content.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No package installation, remote payload retrieval, hooks, services, or automatic execution were found; metadata declares curl and OPENAI_API_KEY as requirements.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions are narrow and contain no prompt hijacking or hidden agent-control behavior; the external upload is stated through the OpenAI API/endpoint wording, though a plainer privacy warning would improve clarity.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact does not create persistence, request elevated privileges, modify agent behavior, or write credentials; it only mentions an optional existing ClawDBot config location for the API key.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The documented purpose is transcription through OpenAI's audio transcriptions endpoint, and the script only reads the caller-provided audio file, sends it to that endpoint, and writes the transcript output.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this only if you are comfortable sending the audio files you choose, plus any prompt/language/model fields, to OpenAI using your API key. Avoid sensitive or regulated recordings unless your policy allows that external processing.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The skill tells users to invoke a local shell script, which is visible in the quick start and consistent with the curl-based purpose; this is a transparency note rather than evidence of hidden execution.\n[SQP-2] expected: The documentation identifies OpenAI's transcription endpoint, so remote processing is purpose-aligned, but the user-facing text should more explicitly say that audio is uploaded off-host.\n[SQP-2] expected: The script's curl request uploads the selected audio file to OpenAI as part of transcription; this is expected behavior for the skill, with the same recommendation for clearer notice.\n[E1] expected: The external transmission to api.openai.com is confirmed and is the core function of the skill, not unrelated exfiltration.\n[T09] unexpected: I reviewed and tested the reported optional-argument expansion; Bash preserves the prompt and language values as single form arguments in this construct, so the stated curl option-splitting issue is not supported by the artifact. The script could still be hardened with validation or safer curl form handling.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013665129}}}}}